      "title": "Alan Saltiel Lab – University of California, San Diego",
      "headings": [
        "ALAN SALTIEL LAB",
        "About Saltiel Laboratory"
      ],
      "text": "ALAN SALTIEL LAB UNDERSTANDING ENERGY METABOLISM IN HEALTH AND DISEASE About Saltiel Laboratory Our lab investigates how metabolically active cells control energy storage and utilization in response to hormones and nutrients in health and disease. For more information, please visit our Research page About Dr. Alan R. Saltiel Dr. Alan R. Saltiel is a Distinguished Professor of Medicine and Pharmacology at UC San Diego and Director of the Institute for Diabetes and Metabolic Health. His research focuses on the molecular mechanisms of insulin action and their role in metabolic diseases, including obesity and diabetes. With over 300 publications and 19 patents, Dr. Saltiel has significantly advanced our understanding of metabolic regulation and has contributed to the development of drugs for diabetes and cancer. FOLLOW US ON TWITTER! Twitter Saltiel lab’s research was in part supported by a generous in-kind contribution of bioreagents from Selleck Chemicals.",
